-- title:
--   Supersingular fibre dictionary with Γ₀(M') relabelling
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q\ge 5$ is a prime, $M'$ is a nonzero natural number with $q\nmid M'$, and $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ satisfying `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$. Write $\kappa_A=\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$.
--
--   **Supersingular places and the constant reduction.** $W$ is a finite set of places of the field $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,\kappa_A\,M'$ over $\kappa_A$ (this field being $\kappa_A(j(q),j(q^{M'}))$ inside $\kappa_A((q))$), and `hW` says that $W$ consists exactly of the places in $\mathrm{ssPlaces}\,q\,M'\,\kappa_A$, that is, of the places $w$ which are rational, satisfy the predicate `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and for which the value $w.\mathrm{evalAt}(\mathrm{jGeomGen})$ lies in `ssJSet q`. The hypothesis `hle` requires $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'\le\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$: the subfield of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$ generated over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ by the coefficientwise images of the full level-$M'$ modular function field over $\mathbb Q$ (generated by the series $j(q^d)$ for $d\mid M'$) is contained in the function field over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of $X_H$ of level $q^2M'$, where $H$ is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$. Next, $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ from $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ to $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,\kappa_A\,M'$: a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ of the source, a surjective residue homomorphism onto the target whose kernel is the maximal ideal of that subring, and a map on places; the axioms require that $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-constants lie in the integers exactly when they lie in $A$ and reduce via $A\to\kappa_A$, that every nonzero element can be scaled by a constant into the integers with nonzero residue, and that the place map preserves degrees and carries the divisor of a function with nonzero residue to the divisor of its residue. The hypothesis `hR₀` requires that this reduction is coefficientwise: for every $y\in A((q))$ whose image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$ lies in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$, that image lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its residue, read as a Laurent series over $\kappa_A$, is obtained from $y$ by reducing coefficients modulo the maximal ideal of $A$. Finally $s$ is a chosen element of $W$, a supersingular place.
--
--   **The arithmetic base.** $k_0$ is an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and $\pi_0\in k_0$ has image in $A$; put $A_0:=A\cap k_0$ (formally `A.comap (algebraMap k₀ (AlgebraicClosure ℚ))`) and $\kappa:=\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A_0$. The hypotheses `hdvr`, `hunif`, `hhens`, `hres` state that $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring whose maximal ideal is generated by $\pi_0$, that $A_0$ is a Henselian local ring, and that $\kappa$ is algebraically closed; `hκ` states that every element of $A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0$ lying in $A$.
--
--   **The auxiliary prime and the function field.** $\ell'$ is a prime with $\ell'\ne q$, $\ell'\ge 3$ and $\ell'\nmid M'$; $\xi\in k_0$ is a primitive $(q\ell')$-th root of unity, and `hιξ` provides a ring homomorphism $\iota:k_0\to\mathbb C$ with $\iota\xi=e^{2\pi i/(q\ell')}$. The field $K$ is an intermediate field of $k_0((q))/k_0$ equal (by `hK`) to the $k_0$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise images of the $\mathbb Q$-rational $q$-expansions of the functions on $X_H$ of level $(q\ell')^2M'$, where now $H=\mathrm{levelH}\,(q\ell')\,M'$ is the kernel of $(\mathbb Z/(q\ell')^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q\ell')^\times$, the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q\ell'$. It is assumed that $K$ is an $A_0$-algebra compatibly with $k_0$, and $j\in K$ is an element whose Laurent expansion is the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion $\mathrm{jq}$ of the modular $j$-invariant, with $j\ne 0$. Write $C'=\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A_0\,K\,j$, the $A_0$-subalgebra of $K$ of elements integral over $A_0[j]$.
--
--   **Functoriality of the level data (hypotheses `hℓ`, `hM`).** For every $A_0$-algebra $T$, every Weierstrass curve over $T$, every variable change $C$ and every `LevelPData`, being a level-$\ell'$ structure is preserved by $C$ and the transported datum is `D.variableChange C`; likewise `IsGamma0PowAt W p k h` implies `IsGamma0PowAt (C • W) p k (kernelVariableChangeDeg C (gamma0PowDeg p k) h)`.
--
--   **Group laws and Drinfeld transport.** $\mathcal G$ is a family `GroupLaws A₀` of relative group laws on the projective models of Weierstrass curves with invertible discriminant over $A_0$-algebras, with `h𝒢` asserting that each is chord–tangent (it admits a compatible points-evaluation) and `h𝒢O` that the identity section is the origin section in the origin chart, with $x/y$ and $z/y$ mapping to $0$. $\mathcal T$ is a `LevelTransport A₀ 𝒢 q`, a functorial transport of raw pairs of sections along $A_0$-algebra maps and variable changes preserving the property of being a Drinfeld $q$-basis, and `h𝒯` is `IsSectionTransport`: the transported sections recover the original ones after composition with the canonical maps induced by a variable change, respectively by a coefficient change. The hypotheses `hVC` and `hCO` assert the existence, in each case, of a graded ring homomorphism between the graded coordinate rings of the projective models realising a given variable change, respectively a given coefficient change, and satisfying the stated inclusion of irrelevant ideals.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Let $Y$ denote the set of maximal ideals $y$ of $C'$ containing the image of $\pi_0$, i.e. the closed points of $\mathrm{Spec}\,C'$ above the closed point of $\mathrm{Spec}\,A_0$, and let $\mathcal R=\mathrm{rigidDataPow}\,A_0\,\ell'\,M'\,q\,h\ell\,hM\,\mathcal G\,\mathcal T$, so that $\mathcal R.\mathrm{Raw}\,\kappa$ consists of a Weierstrass curve over $\kappa$ with invertible discriminant together with a level datum in three parts — a family of polynomials indexed by the prime factors of $M'$ satisfying `IsGamma0PowAt` at the corresponding prime power, a `LevelPData` which is a level-$\ell'$ structure, and a raw pair of sections forming a Drinfeld $q$-basis for $\mathcal G$ — and $\mathcal R.\mathrm{Pt}\,\kappa$ is the quotient of $\mathcal R.\mathrm{Raw}\,\kappa$ modulo the relation generated by the variable-change action. The assertion is that there exists a map $\Phi:Y\to\mathcal R.\mathrm{Raw}\,\kappa$ with the following four properties.
--
--   For $y\in Y$ write $(\ast_y)$ for the condition: for every $g\in\mathbb Q((q))$ belonging to $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFull}\,M'$ whose image in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, such that $g$ has non-negative order at every place of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at which $\mathrm{jq}$ has non-negative order, and such that the residue $R_0.\mathrm{residue}(g)$ lies in the valuation subring of the place $s$: if $\mathrm{qExpand}\,k_0\,\ell'$ applied to the coefficientwise image of $g$ lies in $K$ and the resulting element of $K$ lies in $C'$, then for every $c\in k_0$ whose image lies in $A$ and whose residue in $\kappa_A$ equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}(R_0.\mathrm{residue}(g))$, the difference in $C'$ between that element and the image of $c$ lies in $y$. (Thus $(\ast_y)$ says that $y$ lies over the supersingular place $s$.)
--
--   (i) For every $y\in Y$ satisfying $(\ast_y)$, the affine curve $(\Phi y).\mathrm{curve}$ over $\kappa$ has no nonzero point killed by $q$: if $q\cdot P=0$ then $P=0$.
--
--   (ii) For all $y,y'\in Y$ satisfying $(\ast_y)$ and $(\ast_{y'})$ respectively, there is a variable change $C_0$ over $\kappa$ such that $(\mathcal R.\mathrm{act}\,C_0\,(\Phi y)).\mathrm{curve}=(\Phi y').\mathrm{curve}$, the $\Gamma_0$-power components of the level data agree, $(\mathcal R.\mathrm{act}\,C_0\,(\Phi y)).\mathrm{level}.1=(\Phi y').\mathrm{level}.1$, and the Weil pairing $\mathrm{weilPairing0}$ of index $\ell'$ on $(\Phi y').\mathrm{curve}$, evaluated on the pair of points obtained from the coordinates $(x_P,y_P)$ and $(x_Q,y_Q)$ of the level-$\ell'$ datum of $\mathcal R.\mathrm{act}\,C_0\,(\Phi y)$, coincides with its value on the pair of points obtained from the level-$\ell'$ datum of $\Phi y'$ (the points being formed by `LevelRelabelling.toPoint` on the base change of $(\Phi y').\mathrm{curve}$ to $\kappa$).
--
--   (iii) For every $\gamma\in SL_2(\mathbb Z)$ lying in $\Gamma_0(M')$ and every $k_0$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ such that $\mathrm{IsLevelAutAt}\,k_0\,(q\ell')\,\xi\,(q\ell')\,((q\ell')^2M')\,(\mathrm{levelH}\,(q\ell')\,M')\,\gamma^{-1}\,K\,\tau$ holds — that is: for every weight $k$, every pair of modular forms $f,g$ for $\Gamma_H((q\ell')^2M')$ of weight $k$ with integral $q$-expansion series $p_f,p_g$, $p_g$ having nonzero image, every $x\in K$ whose Laurent expansion is the coefficientwise image of $p_f/p_g$ and every embedding $\iota:k_0\to\mathbb C$ with $\iota\xi=e^{2\pi i/(q\ell')}$, the product of the complex Laurent series $\iota(\tau x)$ with the $q$-expansion of $g\mid_k\mathrm{conjElemN}\,(q\ell')\,\gamma^{-1}$ equals the $q$-expansion of $f\mid_k\mathrm{conjElemN}\,(q\ell')\,\gamma^{-1}$ — and such that $\tau$ maps $C'$ into $C'$: there exists $\gamma''\in SL_2(\mathbb Z)$ with $\gamma''=\gamma$ or $\gamma''=\gamma^{-1}$ such that for all $y,y_1\in Y$ with the transport property that for every $b\in C'$ with $\tau b\in C'$ one has $b\in y$ if and only if $\tau b\in y_1$, and for all raw data $x,x_1\in\mathcal R.\mathrm{Raw}\,\kappa$ and every proof that the discriminant of the curve underlying the Drinfeld pair of $x$ is a unit: if the class of $x$ in $\mathcal R.\mathrm{Pt}\,\kappa$ equals the class of $\Phi y$, and $x_1$ has the same curve as $x$, the same $\Gamma_0$-power component, its level-$\ell'$ datum equal to $\mathrm{LevelPData.relabel}$ of that of $x$ by the integral matrix $\gamma''$, and its Drinfeld pair equal to $\mathrm{RawDrinfeldPair.relabel}\,\mathcal G$ of that of $x$ by $\gamma''$, then the class of $\Phi y_1$ in $\mathcal R.\mathrm{Pt}\,\kappa$ equals the class of $x_1$.
--
--   (iv) For all $y,y'\in Y$, if $(\ast_{y'})$ holds and the classes of $\Phi y$ and $\Phi y'$ in $\mathcal R.\mathrm{Pt}\,\kappa$ are equal, then $y=y'$.
--
--   This is the dictionary between the closed points of the special fibre of the $j$-chart $\mathrm{Spec}\,C'$ of the integral model of $X_H$ at the prime above $q$ and the moduli data over $\kappa$ — an elliptic curve with Drinfeld $q$-basis, level-$\ell'$ structure and $\Gamma_0(M')$-structure — with supersingularity of the curves over the chosen supersingular place $s$, compatibility up to variable change and Weil pairing, equivariance for every level automorphism attached to an element of $\Gamma_0(M')$, and injectivity of the dictionary. It is used in [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelAut_sub_self_mem_of_isLevelAutAt_of_mem_Gamma_of_over_ssPlace_rigidDataPow`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelAut_sub_self_mem_of_isLevelAutAt_of_mem_Gamma_of_over_ssPlace_rigidDataPow), in the analysis of the action of the level automorphisms on the supersingular points of the special fibre.
